{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.OfAssociative","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Basic"],"declarations":59,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kz_sl2_curvature_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kz_sl2_curvature_zero","kind":"theorem","line":799,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L799-L803","doc":"**The `𝔰𝔩₂` KZ connection is flat on `n` points, for every `n`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":785,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L785-L797","doc":"The `𝔰𝔩₂` KZ residues satisfy the infinitesimal pure braid relations, every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue_symm","kind":"theorem","line":782,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L782-L783","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.kzResidue","kind":"def","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L754-L756","doc":"The `𝔰𝔩₂` KZ residue `s_{ij} − ½` in `k[S_n]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.casimir_curvature_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.casimir_curvature_zero","kind":"theorem","line":728,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L728-L736","doc":"**Every KZ-type connection is flat, for every `n`.** For a Lie algebra `L` over a field `k`\nof characteristic zero, an invariant symmetric `Ω ∈ L ⊗ L`, and slot representations `ρ`, the\nconnection `ω = Σ_{i<j} Ω_{ij} d log(z_i − z_j)` has `ω ∧ ω = 0` on the configuration space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.curvature_zero_iff_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.curvature_zero_iff_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L715-L722","doc":"**Flatness ⇔ the infinitesimal pure braid relations, for every `n`.** For symmetric residues\nwhose diagonal entries are central, `ω ∧ ω = 0` on all of configuration space iff the residues\nsatisfy the relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.isFlat_of_curvature_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.isFlat_of_curvature_zero","kind":"theorem","line":668,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L668-L713","doc":"**Flat ⇒ relations, every `n`.** If `ω ∧ ω = 0` at every configuration of distinct points\nfor all tangent vectors, the residues satisfy the infinitesimal pure braid relations. The\ndiagonal residues `M_{ii}` never enter `ω` (`ω_{ii} = 0`), so they are unconstrained by\ncurvature; the relations that mention them hold when they are central (`hdiag`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.disjoint_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.disjoint_commute","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L642-L666","doc":"**Second residue: disjoint commutators vanish.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.natCast_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.natCast_injective","kind":"theorem","line":638,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L638-L640","doc":"The point-sample used to reach configuration space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.residOff_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.residOff_update","kind":"theorem","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L626-L636","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.first_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.first_residue","kind":"theorem","line":582,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L582-L624","doc":"**First residue.** If `[ω(e_i), ω(e_j)] = 0` on all of configuration space, then for every\n`m ∉ {i, j}` the coefficient of the pole at `z_m = z_i` vanishes:\n`[M_{im}, ω(e_j) − (pole at m)] + (z_j − z_i)⁻¹ [M_{im}, M_{jm}] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.resid_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.resid_update","kind":"theorem","line":572,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L572-L580","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.residOff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.residOff","kind":"def","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L568-L570","doc":"`ω(e_a)` with the term at `m` removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.update_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.update_injective","kind":"theorem","line":558,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L558-L566","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.sum_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.sum_split","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L550-L555","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_single","kind":"theorem","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L537-L548","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.resid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.resid","kind":"def","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L534-L535","doc":"`ω(e_a) = Σ_b (z_a − z_b)⁻¹ M_{ab}`: the residue sum at the point `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pole_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pole_two","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L501-L532","doc":"A function of `s` of the form `K₀ + (a − s)⁻¹ K₁ + (b − s)⁻¹ K₂`, `a ≠ b`, vanishing at\nthree distinct points off `{a, b}` has `K₁ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pole_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pole_one","kind":"theorem","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L490-L499","doc":"A function of `s` of the form `K₀ + (a − s)⁻¹ K₁` vanishing at two distinct points\nhas `K₁ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_shift","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L465-L468","doc":"Translation invariance in the base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_dilate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_dilate","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L455-L463","doc":"Homogeneity: `ω` at the dilated point `c·z` is `c⁻¹ ω` at `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_add_euler_translation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_add_euler_translation","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L449-L453","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_add","kind":"theorem","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L441-L447","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.euler_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.euler_commute","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L427-L432","doc":"**The radial component is central for the connection.** For a flat logarithmic\nconnection, `ι_E ω` commutes with `ω(u)` for every tangent vector `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_euler","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L420-L425","doc":"`ι_E ω = ½ Σ_{i ≠ j} M_{ij}`, independent of the point `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_translation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_translation","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L416-L418","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm_smul","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L408-L414","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_euler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_euler","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L402-L406","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.curvature_zero_of_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.curvature_zero_of_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L362-L390","doc":"**Flatness for every `n`.** For symmetric residues satisfying the infinitesimal pure\nbraid relations, `(ω ∧ ω)(u, v) = 0` at every configuration of distinct points, for all\ntangent vectors `u, v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.orbit_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.orbit_zero","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L318-L360","doc":"**The three-point curvature vanishes** for every triple, given the relations, symmetric\nresidues and distinct coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.orbit","kind":"def","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L311-L314","doc":"The `S₃`-orbit of a triple summand: the three-point curvature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.arnold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.arnold","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L299-L309","doc":"**Arnold relation** at a configuration with `z_a, z_b, z_c` distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega_eq_tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega_eq_tri","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L256-L295","doc":"`ω ∧ ω` is the triple sum `Σ_{a,b,c} ω_{ab}(u) ω_{ac}(v) [M_{ab}, M_{ac}]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.term_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.term_split","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L233-L254","doc":"**Term split.** Each term of `ω ∧ ω` equals the sum of its four \"shared index\" parts:\ndisjoint pairs vanish by the first relation, and a pair of pairs sharing both indices gives a\nzero commutator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.tri","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L224-L225","doc":"The triple summand `f(a, b, c) = ω_{ab}(u) ω_{ac}(v) [M_{ab}, M_{ac}]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L207-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.term","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L203-L205","doc":"One term of `ω ∧ ω`: `ω_{ij}(u) ω_{lm}(v) [M_{ij}, M_{lm}]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaWedgeOmega","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L199-L201","doc":"The quadratic part of the curvature, `(ω ∧ ω)(u, v) = ω(u)ω(v) − ω(v)ω(u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.connForm","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L195-L197","doc":"The connection form `ω(u) = ½ Σ_{i,j} ω_{ij}(u) M_{ij}` (`= Σ_{i<j}` for symmetric `M`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_self","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L192-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt_symm","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L189-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.omegaAt","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L186-L187","doc":"`d log(z_i − z_j)` at `z`, on the tangent vector `u`. On the diagonal it is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.casimir_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.casimir_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L164-L174","doc":"**The infinitesimal pure braid relations for every `n`**, from invariance of `Ω` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commute_third_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commute_third_slot","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L158-L162","doc":"`Ω_{ij}` commutes with anything acting only in a third slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commute_slot_coproduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commute_slot_coproduct","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L151-L156","doc":"With `Ω` invariant, `Ω_{ij}` commutes with the coproduct image `ρ_i z + ρ_j z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commutator_slot_coproduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.commutator_slot_coproduct","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L130-L149","doc":"**Invariance in slots `i, j`.** The commutator of `ρ_i z + ρ_j z` with `Ω_{ij}` is the\nimage of `(ad z ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ ad z) Ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.omega","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L127-L128","doc":"The residue `Ω_{ij} = (ρ_i ⊗ ρ_j)(Ω)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.slot_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.slot_comm","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Different slots commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.map_lie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.map_lie","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Each `ρ i` is a Lie map into the commutator algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.ρ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.ρ","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The action in slot `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps.mk","kind":"ctor","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.SlotReps","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L113-L121","doc":"Lie representations of `L` in `n` slots of one algebra, commuting across slots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.IsInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.IsInvariant","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L110-L111","doc":"`Ω` is invariant: it commutes with the coproduct, `(ad z ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ ad z) Ω = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.adPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.adPair","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L105-L108","doc":"The coproduct action of `z` on `L ⊗ L`: `ad z ⊗ 1 + 1 ⊗ ad z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.commute_pairOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.commute_pairOp","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L97-L103","doc":"If `a` commutes with every `f u` and every `g v`, it commutes with `(f ⊗ g)(Ω)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L90-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp_tmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp_tmul","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L87-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.pairOp","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L83-L85","doc":"`(f ⊗ g)(Ω)` read in `A`: the bilinear map `(u, v) ↦ f u * g v` applied to `Ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.IsFlatLogConnection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InfinitesimalPureBraid.IsFlatLogConnection","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InfinitesimalPureBraid.lean#L67-L74","doc":"The infinitesimal pure braid relations on a family of residues (the same predicate as\n`QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.IsFlatLogConnection`, restated so this library file does not import\na content-block sibling). ","signatureChunk":0}]}